  "question": {
    "text": "The main scale of a Vernier Callipers reads in millimeter and its vernier is divided into <math><mn>10</mn></math> divisions which coincides with <math><mn>9</mn></math> divisions of the main scale. The length of the object for situation is found to be <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math> . Find the value of <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi></math> .<br />\r<br />\r<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/nta_abhyas/jee_main/images/81fa0f41-934b-4a47-b088-464d4321430e.png\" style=\"max-width:100%; object-fit:contain\" style=\"height: 204px; width: 200px;\" />",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "5.20",
  "solution": {
    "text": "List count <math><mo>=</mo><mn>0.1</mn></math> <math><mi mathvariant=\"italic\">m</mi><mi mathvariant=\"italic\">m</mi></math><br />Negative zero error <math><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant=\"italic\">L</mi><mi mathvariant=\"italic\">C</mi><mo>×</mo><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>10</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>9</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>0.1</mn></math> <math><mi mathvariant=\"italic\">m</mi><mi mathvariant=\"italic\">m</mi></math><br />Measured value <math><mo>=</mo><mn>5.0</mn><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant=\"italic\">L</mi><mi mathvariant=\"italic\">C</mi><mo>×</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo></math> negative<br />Zero error <math><mo>=</mo><mn>5.20</mn></math>",
